### ===============================
### API SECURITY - FULL (v0.1.25)
### ===============================

### ===== TWO-FACTOR AUTHENTICATION (2FA) =====

### 1. Enable 2FA
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Response includes:
# - qrCodeDataUrl: Base64 PNG image (scan with Google Authenticator / Authy)
# - manualEntryKey: Manual entry for authenticator app
# - backupCodes: [10 codes] - SAVE THESE SECURELY!

### 2. Verify 2FA Code (TOTP)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456",
  "isBackupCode": false
}

### 3. Verify 2FA Code (Backup Code)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "ABCD1234",
  "isBackupCode": true
}

### 4. Generate New Backup Codes
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/backup-codes
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5. Disable 2FA
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ===== API KEY MANAGEMENT =====

### 6. Create API Key (Full Permissions)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Production Integration",
  "description": "API key for production server integration",
  "rateLimitPerMinute": 120,
  "expiresAt": "2026-12-31T23:59:59Z",
  "permissions": [
    "/api/v1/invoices/*",
    "/api/v1/customers/*",
    "/api/v1/products/*"
  ],
  "allowedIps": [
    "203.0.113.0",
    "198.51.100.0"
  ]
}

### Response will include the actual API key - SAVE IT!
### Format: acc_os_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

### 7. Create API Key (Read-Only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/api-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Read-Only Reporting",
  "description": "Read-only access for external reporting",
  "rateLimitPerMinute": 60,
  "permissions": [
    "GET /api/v1/invoices",
    "GET /api/v1/reports/*"
  ]
}

### 8. Revoke API Key
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/api-keys/{{apiKeyId}}/revoke
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ===== RATE LIMITING TESTS =====

### 9. Test Normal Request (Within Limit)
GET {{baseUrl}}/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Check response headers:
# X-RateLimit-Remaining: Shows remaining requests

### 10. Test Rate Limit (Make Multiple Requests)
# Make 1001 requests in 1 minute to trigger global rate limit
# Or make 6 login attempts in 5 minutes to trigger login rate limit

### ===== SECURITY HEADERS VERIFICATION =====

### 11. Verify Security Headers
GET {{baseUrl}}/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Expected Response Headers:
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
# X-Frame-Options: DENY
# X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
# Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
# Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; ...
# Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains (HTTPS only)
# Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

### ===== 2FA WORKFLOW =====

### 12. Complete 2FA Setup Workflow

# Step 1: Enable 2FA
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

# Step 2: Scan QR code with Google Authenticator
# Or manually enter the key shown in response

# Step 3: Verify with first TOTP code
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456",
  "isBackupCode": false
}

# Step 4: Save backup codes securely!

### 13. Use Backup Code (One-Time)
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "ABCD1234",
  "isBackupCode": true
}

### 14. Regenerate Backup Codes
POST {{baseUrl}}/security/2fa/backup-codes
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ===== API KEY USAGE =====

### 15. Use API Key for Request
GET {{baseUrl}}/invoices
X-API-Key: acc_os_your_api_key_here

### 16. API Key with Rate Limiting
# API key has its own rate limit (rateLimitPerMinute)
# Make requests exceeding the limit

GET {{baseUrl}}/invoices
X-API-Key: acc_os_your_api_key_here

### ===== BRUTE FORCE PROTECTION =====

### 17. Test Failed Login Protection
# Make 5 failed login attempts from same IP

POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "wrong_password_1"
}

# After 5th attempt, IP will be auto-blacklisted for 30 minutes
# Status: 429 Too Many Requests

